{title: With All My Heart}
{subtitle: Psalms 9:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 74}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] [Bb/F] | [Eb] [Bb/D] |
| [Fsus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I will thank the LORD with all my [Eb]heart
[Gm7]I will tell [F]of all your won[Bb]ders
You are the Most High, [F/A]the judge [Eb]of earth
My [Gm7]enemies turn [F]back and lose their [Bb]grounders
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
They [Eb]stumble and [F]perish [Bb]before your [Eb]face
You have [F]upheld my [Gm]right in this place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With [Bb]all my [F/A]heart I sing your [Gm]praise
[Eb]Rejoicing in [F]the joy of your [Bb]days
[Eb]I will tell of [F]all your won[Gm]ders
With [F]all my heart I [Eb]stand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You [Bb]have taken your [F/A]seat on the [Eb]throne
A [Gm]righteous judge [F]who is [Bb]known
My [Gm]cause is up[F]held in your [Eb]light
My [Gm]enemies [F]are gone from [Bb]sight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
They [Eb]stumble and [F]perish [Gm]before your face
[Eb]You have [F]upheld my [Gm]right in this place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With [Bb]all my [F/A]heart I sing your [Gm]praise
[Eb]Rejoicing in [F]the joy of your [Bb]days
[Eb]I will tell of all [F]your won[Gm]ders
With [F]all my heart I [Eb]stand
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm]Glad and re[F]joice in you a[Eb]lone
[Gm]Your name is [F]holy, [Eb]your love is known
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
With [Bb]all my [F/A]heart I sing your [Gm]praise
[Eb]Rejoicing in [F]the joy of your [Bb]days
[Eb]I will tell of [F]all your won[Gm]ders
With [F]all my heart I [Eb]stand [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}
